.TH FAMILIA 1 "" "familia" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
familia \- topology coordinator for local LLMs on old hardware: menu and command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B familia
.br
.B familia
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIVALUE\fR...] [\fIARG\fR...]
.br
.B familia help
[\fICOMMAND\fR | \fB\-\-man\fR]
.br
.B familia search
\fIWORD\fR [\fB\-\-run\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B familia
\fBlist\fR | \fBrun\fR \fIKEY\fR | \fBmenu\fR | \fBcompletion bash\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments, \fBfamilia\fR opens the menu, grouped by task, where every item shows the exact command it runs. Every menu item is also a command: \fBfamilia\fR \fICOMMAND\fR runs the same command as the menu, with the same license review and the same prompts. Values the command needs (shown as \fI<NAME>\fR) are taken from the arguments in order, or from the flag that precedes them in the command (for example \fB\-\-agent\fR \fIhermes\fR); missing values are asked for on a terminal, a default is used when there is one, otherwise the command stops with exit status 2. Any further arguments are passed to the underlying script unchanged.
.PP
On Windows the same commands are run with \fBfamilia.cmd\fR; commands that only exist on one platform are left out on the other.
.PP
Commands marked (licenses first) run \fBscripts/licenses.py gate\fR before anything is installed, started or fetched. Nothing is accepted for you: on a terminal you are asked, without one the command stops unless \fB\-\-yes\fR is given.
